    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1043">

                <pb facs="0876" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Gleysteen, Culver: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Paddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-16T01:00:00+09:00">April 16, 1949—1
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:27 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>109. Chief Soviet Kommandatura today said I receive 2 or 3 days answer to points
                    re Gleysteen arrest (reference immediately preceding telegram); thus no need
                    action last paragraph as yet.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 109; repeated Nanking 75, Moscow 6.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paddock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
